<report>
<title>Normal distribution (z) test - single sample</title>
<table>
<tr><td>Sample name:</td><td>@name</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sample mean = </td><td>@mean</td></tr>
<tr><td>Population mean =</td><td>@pop_mean</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sample size n =</td><td>@size</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sample sd =</td><td>@sd</td></tr>
<tr><td>Population sd =</td><td>@psd</td></tr>
</table>

<p><ci>@pc% confidence interval @for = @from to @to</ci></p>

<p>Standard normal deviate (z) = @z<br />
<pval>One sided @{p_1:pval}</pval><br />
<pval>Two sided @{p_2:pval}</pval></p>

<p>For lognormal data:<br />
<subtotal>Geometric mean = @gmean  (@pc2% confidence interval = @lrr to @urr)</subtotal></p>
<block name="warn">

<p><warn>WARNING: numbers too small for this test, consider using a Student t test instead</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
